From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
Date: Mon, 21 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] test: tolerate a host with no /var/log/syslog

collect_logs() is called from Variant.prepare_result() after every single
austin invocation, and on Linux it opens /var/log/syslog unconditionally. That
file is an rsyslog artefact: a journald-only host (Fedora, RHEL, Rocky, Arch,
or a minimal Ubuntu image like the self-hosted riscv64 runners) has none, so
the helper raises before the test under it can assert anything:

    test/utils.py:154: in collect_logs
        with Path("/var/log/syslog").open(errors="replace") as logfile:
    E   FileNotFoundError: [Errno 2] No such file or directory: '/var/log/syslog'

    ================== 40 failed, 27 skipped in 512.75s (0:08:32) ==================

Every failure in that run was this line; nothing about austin was exercised.
Return no logs when the file is absent, which is what the macOS branch below
already does, and leave the diagnostics untouched where rsyslog is installed.

Upstream-Status: To upstream [not yet submitted]

Signed-off-by: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
---
diff --git a/test/utils.py b/test/utils.py
--- a/test/utils.py
+++ b/test/utils.py
@@ -151,7 +151,12 @@ def collect_logs(variant: str, pid: int) -> List[str]:
     needles: tuple[str, ...]
     match platform.system():
         case "Linux":
-            with Path("/var/log/syslog").open(errors="replace") as logfile:
+            syslog = Path("/var/log/syslog")
+            if not syslog.is_file():
+                # Not every Linux host has rsyslog; on a journald-only system
+                # there is no file to grep for austin's messages.
+                return []
+            with syslog.open(errors="replace") as logfile:
                 needles = (f"{variant}[{pid}]", f"systemd-coredump[{pid}]")
                 return [
                     f" logs for {variant}[{pid}] ".center(80, "="),
